  "verbalization": "CDP-Ethanolamine is implicated in the target relationship with ZR-75-1 through a series of molecular interactions involving SNU-387. The evidence suggests that CDP-Ethanolamine acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Tetraethylammonium and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. These compounds are all linked to ZR-75-1, indicating a potential pathway where CDP-Ethanolamine may influence ZR-75-1 through the activation or modulation of SNU-387. The presence of multiple targets for SNU-387 suggests a possible mechanism of action involving receptor or enzyme interaction, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where CDP-Ethanolamine is a central node in a network of targets leading to ZR-75-1, highlighting the importance of SNU-387 in mediating this relationship.",
